    Add the file-ticket and respond-to-user agents
    
    Two steps of the resolution loop that were mocked now have working
    implementations in the repo, registered in TrueForge by npm run provision and
    callable directly by the API.
    
    file-ticket reconstructs what a template cannot: repro steps, expected versus
    actual, and acceptance criteria, taken from what the reporters actually wrote.
    Its instructions forbid inventing a step nobody described, because a plausible
    invented step gets a real bug closed as cannot-reproduce.
    
    respond-to-user writes the reply in the venue's register, in two distinct
    phases. Acknowledgement goes out before anything is fixed and must not imply
    otherwise; the follow-up asks the reporter to check rather than asserting the
    fix works, because only they can establish that.
    
    Both separate drafting from sending. Drafting is free and reversible. Filing
    writes to someone's backlog and replying is speech in the company's name to a
    named person on a platform where it cannot be unsaid, so submitTicket and
    deliverReply are gates rather than omissions. The loop's promise that no staff
    member has to act survives a gate, since a gate is a policy set once rather
    than a person reviewing each message.
    
    Closing stays exclusive to the reporter: /confirm is the only route that can
    close an issue and it requires their actual words, since an audit trail is
    worth nothing if 'the reporter confirmed' can be recorded without what they
    said.
    
    npm run trueforge starts TrueForge and npm run provision waits for it and
    registers every agent, so a fresh checkout can populate itself.
    
