    Write one verdict over the whole window, and batch the abuse stage
    
    The first run that completed every model stage exposed both of these.
    
    The verdict argued with itself — 'drifting negative, and the pull is growing
    steeper' followed immediately by 'flat-to-slightly-positive' — because the
    batch verdicts were concatenated, and each batch had only seen four items and
    generalised from them. A verdict is a claim about the whole window, so it is
    now written by one pass that can see the whole window, reasoning over the
    tallies, the common themes and the most extreme items rather than the full
    corpus.
    
    Abuse was the last un-batched model call and duly timed out, losing the stage
    and returning no findings. Ten candidates per turn completes, and a failed
    batch now costs only its own ten.
    
