    Replace the agentic fetch pipeline with deterministic search
    
    Every stage returned empty while the UI reported "done". Six causes, each
    hiding the next:
    
    - runStage caught stage errors without rethrowing, so index.ts set
      status:'done' unconditionally. A scan where all six stages failed was
      presented as a completed scan with six empty panels. A run that produces
      nothing is now an error, and a partial run says which section is short.
    
    - Retrieval ran through an LLM tool-calling loop. Underneath it is a handful
      of HTTP requests, so presence/discovery/feed now issue them directly
      (app/server/search.ts). resolveSite is one search rather than an agent turn.
    
    - TrueForge cannot produce schema-constrained JSON from a custom provider:
      with tools attached llama.cpp returns 400 "failed to parse grammar" (a
      json_schema grammar and a tool grammar cannot compile together), and with
      tools off the schema is ignored and the model answers in prose. Buzz,
      health and abuse call the endpoint directly instead (app/server/model.ts).
      TrueForge injects built-in tools when dynamicSubAgents/generativeUi are on,
      so those are now off for the reasoning agents.
    
    - The provider URL pointed at a proxy that accepts response_format, forwards
      the request without it, and returns prose with finish_reason "stop" — a
      silently dropped schema. LLM_BASE_URL overrides it.
    
    - Buzz and health emitted their whole result in one turn, breaching the 4k
      output cap. Both are batched now; a failed batch costs only itself.
    
    - Sentiment and triage reasoned over Brave meta descriptions, not over what
      anyone wrote. That is why four copies of the same "best alternatives"
      listicle scored -0.30/-0.20/0.00/0.00 and why triage found no complaints
      in sixty mentions. app/server/content.ts fetches real page text (HN yields
      full comment threads), discovery adds complaint-language queries, and
      dictionary/spelling results are dropped for brands that are ordinary words.
    
    Reddit blocks this network on every route and its .env credentials are empty,
    so those mentions keep their snippet and are flagged isFullText:false rather
    than passed off as someone's words. Bright Data is wired as the escape hatch
    for blocked pages, gated on BRIGHTDATA_API_TOKEN.
    
    Also: drop the reddit and linkedin connectors, using exa in linkedin's place;
    send reasoningEffort only to models that advertise support; restore the score
    range in the buzz schema description, since strictify() removes minimum and
    maximum and the model was returning 7 on a -1..1 scale.
    
    Result for "lovable": 22 accounts, 60 mentions, 60 feed items, 17 monthly
    sentiment buckets. Previously zero of each.
    
